{"step_index":2702,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T12:54:12Z","input_tokens":183246,"cache_read_tokens":0,"output_tokens":3055,"content":"# Phase 7 Implementation Report: 10-Stage Beginner DSA Roadmap\n\nI have implemented and verified **Phase 7: Build a Beginner Roadmap** inside your **Teach Me This Code** DSA learning platform.\n\nThe roadmap provides a structured progression from Python fundamentals to advanced competitive data structures. It gives learners the freedom to **skip stages, revisit concepts anytime, jump to any problem, and designate their own active focus stage** without artificial locks, paywalls, or AI dependencies.\n\n---\n\n## 1. The 10-Stage Learning Order & Curriculum\n\nThe 10 stages cover **all 30 topics** in the curated catalog.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n  S1[\"Stage 1: Python Fundamentals & Arrays<br/><i>(Arrays • Slicing • In-place Swapping)</i>\"]\n  S2[\"Stage 2: Strings & Hashing<br/><i>(Strings • Hash Maps • Frequency Dictionaries)</i>\"]\n  S3[\"Stage 3: Two Pointers & Sliding Windows<br/><i>(Converging Pointers • Dynamic Window Horizons)</i>\"]\n  S4[\"Stage 4: Prefix Sums, Sorting & Binary Search<br/><i>(O(1) Range Queries • O(log n) Halving)</i>\"]\n  S5[\"Stage 5: Linked Lists, Stacks & Queues<br/><i>(Pointers • LIFO Matching • Monotonic Stacks)</i>\"]\n  S6[\"Stage 6: Recursion & Backtracking<br/><i>(Call Stacks • Decision Trees • Branch Pruning)</i>\"]\n  S7[\"Stage 7: Trees & Binary Search Trees<br/><i>(DFS/BFS • BST Invariants • Prefix Tries)</i>\"]\n  S8[\"Stage 8: Heaps & Graphs<br/><i>(Priority Queues • BFS Shortest Path • Topological Sort)</i>\"]\n  S9[\"Stage 9: Greedy Algorithms & Dynamic Programming<br/><i>(Memoization • Tabulation • Kadane's Algorithm)</i>\"]\n  S10[\"Stage 10: Advanced Patterns & Data Structures<br/><i>(Bitwise XOR • 2D Matrices • Composite LRU Cache)</i>\"]\n\n  S1 --> S2 --> S3 --> S4 --> S5 --> S6 --> S7 --> S8 --> S9 --> S10\n```\n\n| Stage | Title & Focus | Constituent Topics | Core Milestone Problem | Handpicked Starter Problems |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Stage 1** | **Python fundamentals and arrays** | Arrays | **Two Sum** (LC 1) | Two Sum (`#1`), Contains Duplicate (`#2`), Product of Array (`#6`), Move Zeroes (`#13`) |\n| **Stage 2** | **Strings and hashing** | Strings, Hashing and Hash Maps | **Valid Anagram** (LC 242) & **Group Anagrams** (LC 49) | Valid Anagram (`#3`), Group Anagrams (`#4`), Longest Consecutive Sequence (`#8`), Longest Common Prefix (`#25`) |\n| **Stage 3** | **Two pointers and sliding windows** | Two Pointers, Sliding Window | **3Sum** (LC 15) & **Longest Substring Without Repeating** (LC 3) | Valid Palindrome (`#31`), Two Sum II (`#32`), 3Sum (`#33`), Longest Substring Without Repeating (`#52`) |\n| **Stage 4** | **Prefix sums, sorting, and binary search** | Prefix Sum, Sorting, Binary Search | **Binary Search** (LC 704) & **Search in Rotated Array** (LC 33) | Subarray Sum Equals K (`#16`), Sort Colors (`#22`), Binary Search (`#89`), Search a 2D Matrix II (`#91`) |\n| **Stage 5** | **Linked lists, stacks, and queues** | Linked Lists, Stacks, Queues and Deques, Monotonic Stack & Queue | **Valid Parentheses** (LC 20) & **Reverse Linked List** (LC 206) | Valid Parentheses (`#69`), Min Stack (`#70`), Reverse Linked List (`#109`), Merge Two Sorted Lists (`#110`) |\n| **Stage 6** | **Recursion and backtracking** | Recursion, Backtracking | **Subsets** (LC 78) & **Combination Sum** (LC 39) | Subsets (`#187`), Combination Sum (`#189`), Permutations (`#191`), Word Search (`#193`) |\n| **Stage 7** | **Trees and binary search trees** | Trees and Binary Trees, Binary Search Trees, Tries | **Maximum Depth of Binary Tree** (LC 104) & **Validate BST** (LC 98) | Invert Binary Tree (`#131`), Maximum Depth (`#132`), Kth Smallest in BST (`#143`), Implement Trie (`#163`) |\n| **Stage 8** | **Heaps and graphs** | Heaps and Priority Queues, Graphs, BFS, DFS, Topological Sorting, Union-Find | **Number of Islands** (LC 200) & **Course Schedule** (LC 207) | Kth Largest Element (`#171`), Number of Islands (`#205`), Clone Graph (`#206`), Course Schedule (`#212`) |\n| **Stage 9** | **Greedy algorithms and dynamic programming** | Greedy Algorithms, Dynamic Programming, Intervals | **Climbing Stairs** (LC 70) & **Maximum Subarray** (LC 53) | Climbing Stairs (`#239`), Maximum Subarray (`#251`), House Robber (`#241`), Jump Game (`#281`) |\n| **Stage 10** | **Advanced patterns and data structures** | Advanced Data Structures, Bit Manipulation, Math and Number Theory, Matrix Problems | **Single Number** (LC 136) & **Rotate Image** (LC 48) | Single Number (`#10`), Rotate Image (`#19`), Set Matrix Zeroes (`#20`), Number of 1 Bits (`#295`) |\n\n---\n\n## 2. Freedom to Skip, Revisit & Select Custom Learning Order\n\n- **Zero Artificial Gating or Locks**: Every stage is accessible immediately. Learners can open any problem or inspect any stage.\n- **Active Focus Stage Selector**: Learners can designate their active stage with `🎯 Set as My Focus`. The selection is persisted locally (`localStorage.getItem('dsa_active_stage')`).\n- **Active Stage Spotlight**: Both the Dashboard Overview card and the Roadmap Hero render an Active Stage Focus card displaying real-time metrics (`X / Y Solved`, percentage, and a direct `Continue Stage N →` button).\n- **10-Pill Quick Jump Navigation**: A sticky quick-jump bar with pills 1 through 10 allows one-click smooth scrolling directly to any stage card with a pulse highlight animation.\n- **Stage Filter Bar**: Learners can filter roadmap cards by `All (10 Stages)`, `In Progress`, `Mastered`, or `Not Started`.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Meaningful Completion Rules (Zero Fake Numbers)\n\nIn strict accordance with the non-negotiables:\n1. **Never Mark Mastered on Open**: Simply browsing, viewing in a modal, or opening a workspace **does not** mark a stage or topic as mastered.\n2. **Real Status Derivation**:\n   - `⚪ Not Started`: 0 problems solved and 0 attempted in that stage.\n   - `⏳ In Progress`: At least 1 problem attempted or solved.\n   - `🏆 Mastered`: Earned only when the learner has solved multiple problems ($\\ge 5$), solved at least $50\\%$ of the stage, **and** passed the stage's core milestone problem (or solved $100\\%$ of the stage).\n3. **Automated Test Validation**: Running tests in the workspace and passing 100% of test cases triggers real solved recording (`markSolved`) which updates the stage's progress track in real time.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Problem Library Explorer & Stage Filter Integration\n\n- **Stage Dropdown**: Added a `Stage:` filter selector to the Problem Library toolbar (`All 10 Stages`, `Stage 1: Python Fundamentals & Arrays`, ... `Stage 10: Advanced Patterns & Structures`).\n- **Stage Problem Exploration**: Clicking `📂 Explore All [N] Problems in Stage [X] →` filters the 300 problems table directly to that stage's problems and scrolls into view.\n- **Practice Next Problem**: Clicking `🚀 Practice Next Problem →` computes the first unsolved problem in that stage and opens its workspace.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Files Changed & Created\n\n1. [dsa_dashboard.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/dsa_dashboard.js):\n   - Defined `BEGINNER_ROADMAP_10_STAGES` (10 stages, descriptions, milestones, starters, key concepts).\n   - Added backward compatibility alias `ROADMAP_PHASES = BEGINNER_ROADMAP_10_STAGES`.\n   - Added `loadActiveStage`, `setActiveStage`, `getStageProblems`, `getStageStats`, `practiceNextInStage`, `exploreStageProblems`.\n   - Updated `renderRoadmapOverviewCard` to display all 10 stages with progress tracks and the Active Focus Spotlight.\n   - Updated `renderFullRoadmap` with the 10-stage timeline, KPI summary, quick-jump pills, concept checklists, milestone cards, and starter grids.\n   - Added `selectedStage` filter handling in `filterProblems` / `getFilteredProblems`.\n2. [styles.css](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/styles.css):\n   - Added styling for `.roadmap-kpi-bar`, `.roadmap-jump-pill`, `.card-active-focus`, `.stage-status-badge`, `.stage-concepts-box`, `.stage-milestone-banner`, `.overview-focus-banner`, and `.stage-highlight-pulse`.\n3. [test_dsa_phase7_roadmap.js](file:///C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/brain/4b927fe1-f9a3-4b3f-9f8a-92760e157eef/scratch/test_dsa_phase7_roadmap.js):\n   - Comprehensive test suite covering structure, topic coverage, navigation freedom, completion rules, filter synchronization, and visualizer output verification.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Verification & Test Execution Results\n\nAll 8 test suites passed with **100% success**:\n\n| Test Suite | Purpose | Tests / Result |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **test_dsa_phase7_roadmap.js** | 10 stages, suggested order, completion rules, navigation freedom, milestone verification, Kadane output | **31 / 31 Passed (100%)** |\n| **test_dsa_phase6_solutions.js** | Dual-approach solutions, Big-$O$, offline verification, explanation cards | **2,863 / 2,863 Passed (100%)** |\n| **test_dsa_phase5_workspace.js** | Dedicated workspace (Understand, Pattern, Editor, Visualize), test runner | **101 / 101 Passed (100%)** |\n| **test_dsa_phase4.js** | Search, multi-topic, difficulty, status, sorting, pagination, import duplicate prevention | **43 / 43 Passed (100%)** |\n| **test_dsa_phase3.js** | 300 curated problems, schemas, complexity, starter codes, URLs | **17 / 17 Passed (100%)** |\n| **test_dsa_phase2.js** | 30 topic pages, difficulty distributions, category chips | **40 / 40 Passed (100%)** |\n| **test_dsa_phase1.js** | Dashboard metrics, continue learning, recent sessions, roadmap overview card | **31 / 31 Passed (100%)** |\n| **test_phase5.js** | Code visualizer execution engine, variable tracking, step navigation, Kadane verification | **100% Passed (Output = 6)** |\n\n---\n\n## 7. Next Steps\n\nWith Phase 7 complete, all core requirements of the DSA Learning Platform (Phases 1 through 7) are implemented, integrated, and verified. Would you like to review the UI layout, explore additional problem test cases, or inspect any specific stage?"}
