{"step_index":2740,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-27T13:02:52Z","input_tokens":2091,"cache_read_tokens":214411,"output_tokens":15715,"thinking":"The code ensures that the most recently accessed problem is restored upon returning to the learning environment. The logic prioritizes the `lastOpenedProblemId` for persistence. If that's unavailable, it defaults to the `lastPracticedId` to maintain user context.\n\nI'm thinking through how to approach this.\n\n\nA `DsaIndexedDbBackup` class will manage IndexedDB persistence for application state snapshots. This class will provide methods for saving and loading snapshots to IndexedDB, including error handling. This IndexedDB backup mechanism will store progress snapshots, ensuring user context is preserved.\n\n\nThe `DsaIndexedDbBackup` class's read operation will retrieve persisted snapshots using a transaction and object store request.  If the read is successful, the data payload is resolved; otherwise, the function resolves with null to handle cases of missing data. The operation incorporates a try-catch block for robust error management, resolving with null upon any exception.\n\n\nThe local storage utilizes both `localStorage` and `IndexedDB` for data persistence within the browser environment. Data includes learning progress, code solutions, notes, bookmarks and roadmap achievements. Export and import functionalities are provided to manage data synchronization across devices.\n\n\nIndexedDB will be utilized for storing and restoring learning progress data, including attempts, bookmarks, notes, active stage, and user-saved code solutions. The application presents statistics reflecting the user's progress: problems attempted, bookmarked problems, personal notes, current stage, and saved solutions. These data points must be accurately represented and updated in the user interface.\n\n\nA robust backup mechanism is planned to ensure no data loss. This involves downloading user data as a JSON file.  There is also the option to copy this same data to the clipboard for external saving.\n\n\nA mechanism for importing user data via JSON files and clipboard text will be implemented, providing options for merging or replacing existing data. Verification will be performed on imported data to prevent corruption. The data includes learning progress, code solutions, and user achievements.\n\n\nData import will encompass JSON file and clipboard text input, with the option to merge or replace existing user data. Input validation will be implemented to prevent data corruption during the import process. This process ensures data integrity across different devices.\n\n\nThe application will persist user preferences using configurable options for page size, default sorting method, and code editor font size. These settings will be accessible through a user interface. Default values will be provided if no user-defined preferences exist, and the current settings will be displayed for selection and modification.\n\n\nThe application will offer font size and visualizer playback speed as configurable user preferences accessible through the UI. Default values will be used if user-defined settings are unavailable, with existing selections displayed for modification.\n\n\nModal interactions will be handled to manage progress backups.  Events from closing the modal, downloading backups, copying backup data, and importing data from file or clipboard are defined. File input triggers file reading and validation, while textarea input validates the imported data.  Validation displays success or failure messages and enables/disables the import commit button based on the validation result.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"import re\nimport os\n\ntarget_file = r'C:\\Users\\CVT\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\code-flow-visualizer\\app_build\\dsa_dashboard.js'\nwith open(target_file, 'r', encoding='utf-8') as f:\n    code = f.read()\n\n# 1. Add DsaIndexedDbBackup class definition near the top (after storage constants)\nstorage_constants = \"\"\"  const STORAGE_KEY = 'dsa_learning_progress_v1';\n  const SETTINGS_STORAGE_KEY = 'dsa_learning_settings_v1';\n  const CODE_CACHE_KEY = 'dsa_user_code_v1';\n  const ACTIVE_STAGE_KEY = 'dsa_active_stage';\n\n  // IndexedDB Persistent Backup Layer (Phase 8: Offline Local Storage)\n  class DsaIndexedDbBackup {\n    constructor(dbName = 'TeachMeThisCode_DSA_DB', storeName = 'progress_snapshots') {\n      this.dbName = dbName;\n      this.storeName = storeName;\n      this.db = null;\n      this.init();\n    }\n\n    init() {\n      if (typeof window === 'undefined' || !window.indexedDB) return;\n      try {\n        const req = window.indexedDB.open(this.dbName, 1);\n        req.onupgradeneeded = (e) => {\n          const db = e.target.result;\n          if (!db.objectStoreNames.contains(this.storeName)) {\n            db.createObjectStore(this.storeName, { keyPath: 'key' });\n          }\n        };\n        req.onsuccess = (e) => {\n          this.db = e.target.result;\n        };\n      } catch (e) {\n        // Fallback gracefully in restricted environments\n      }\n    }\n\n    saveSnapshot(key, payload) {\n      if (!this.db) return Promise.resolve(false);\n      return new Promise((resolve) => {\n        try {\n          const tx = this.db.transaction([this.storeName], 'readwrite');\n          const store = tx.objectStore(this.storeName);\n          store.put({ key, payload, updatedAt: Date.now() });\n          tx.oncomplete = () => resolve(true);\n          tx.onerror = () => resolve(false);\n        } catch (e) {\n          resolve(false);\n        }\n      });\n    }\n\n    loadSnapshot(key) {\n      if (!this.db) return Promise.resolve(null);\n      return new Promise((resolve) => {\n        try {\n          const tx = this.db.transaction([this.storeName], 'readonly');\n          const store = tx.objectStore(this.storeName);\n          const req = store.get(key);\n          req.onsuccess = () => resolve(req.result ? req.result.payload : null);\n          req.onerror = () => resolve(null);\n        } catch (e) {\n          resolve(null);\n        }\n      });\n    }\n  }\n\"\"\"\n\nold_key = \"  const STORAGE_KEY = 'dsa_learning_progress_v1';\"\nif old_key in code:\n    code = code.replace(old_key, storage_constants, 1)\n    print(\"[SUCCESS] Added storage constants and DsaIndexedDbBackup class\")\nelse:\n    print(\"[ERROR] STORAGE_KEY not found\")\n\n# 2. Update constructor: initialize indexedDbBackup, settings, lastOpenedProblemId\nconstructor_target = \"\"\"      this.progress = this.loadProgress();\n      this.initDOM();\"\"\"\n\nconstructor_replacement = \"\"\"      this.indexedDbBackup = new DsaIndexedDbBackup();\n      this.settings = this.loadSettings();\n      // Apply preferred learning settings\n      if (this.settings.pageSize) this.pageSize = this.settings.pageSize;\n      if (this.settings.selectedSort) this.selectedSort = this.settings.selectedSort;\n\n      this.progress = this.loadProgress();\n      // Restore last opened problem\n      if (this.progress && this.progress.lastOpenedProblemId) {\n        this.activeWorkspaceProblemId = this.progress.lastOpenedProblemId;\n      } else if (this.progress && this.progress.lastPracticedId) {\n        this.activeWorkspaceProblemId = this.progress.lastPracticedId;\n      }\n\n      this.initDOM();\"\"\"\n\nif constructor_target in code:\n    code = code.replace(constructor_target, constructor_replacement, 1)\n    print(\"[SUCCESS] Updated constructor with Phase 8 persistence state\")\nelse:\n    print(\"[ERROR] constructor_target not found\")\n\n# 3. Add Phase 8 Methods: loadSettings, saveSettings, exportProgressData, downloadProgressBackup, copyProgressBackupToClipboard, validateProgressImport, importProgress, resetProgress, showProgressStorageModal\nphase8_methods = \"\"\"\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    // PHASE 8: LOCAL PROGRESS STORAGE, BACKUP & PREFERENCES\n    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    loadSettings() {\n      const defaultSettings = {\n        pageSize: 25,\n        selectedSort: 'order_asc',\n        codeFontSize: '14px',\n        animationSpeed: 'medium',\n        confirmSolutionReveal: true\n      };\n      try {\n        const raw = localStorage.getItem(SETTINGS_STORAGE_KEY);\n        if (raw) {\n          const parsed = JSON.parse(raw);\n          return Object.assign({}, defaultSettings, parsed);\n        }\n      } catch (e) {}\n      return defaultSettings;\n    }\n\n    saveSettings(newSettings) {\n      this.settings = Object.assign({}, this.settings || {}, newSettings);\n      try {\n        localStorage.setItem(SETTINGS_STORAGE_KEY, JSON.stringify(this.settings));\n      } catch (e) {\n        console.warn('Could not save learning settings to localStorage:', e);\n      }\n      if (this.settings.pageSize) this.pageSize = this.settings.pageSize;\n      if (this.settings.selectedSort) this.selectedSort = this.settings.selectedSort;\n      if (this.indexedDbBackup) {\n        this.indexedDbBackup.saveSnapshot('settings', this.settings);\n      }\n      this.render();\n    }\n\n    exportProgressData() {\n      const stats = this.computeStats();\n      const lastOpenedId = (this.progress && this.progress.lastOpenedProblemId) || this.activeWorkspaceProblemId || 1;\n      const exportPayload = {\n        \"$schema\": \"teach_me_this_code_progress_v1\",\n        \"version\": \"1.0\",\n        \"exportedAt\": Date.now(),\n        \"exportedAtISO\": new Date().toISOString(),\n        \"platform\": \"Teach Me This Code - DSA Learning Hub\",\n        \"notice\": \"All data stored locally on your device. Use Import Progress to transfer between browsers or devices.\",\n        \"stats\": {\n          \"totalCatalog\": this.problems.length,\n          \"solvedCount\": (this.progress.solved || []).length,\n          \"attemptedCount\": (this.progress.attempted || []).length,\n          \"bookmarkedCount\": (this.progress.bookmarked || []).length,\n          \"reviewCount\": (this.progress.review || []).length,\n          \"notesCount\": Object.keys(this.progress.notes || {}).length,\n          \"userCodeCount\": Object.keys(this.userCodeCache || {}).length,\n          \"activeStage\": this.activeStage,\n          \"lastOpenedProblemId\": lastOpenedId\n        },\n        \"progress\": {\n          \"solved\": Array.from(new Set(this.progress.solved || [])),\n          \"attempted\": Array.from(new Set(this.progress.attempted || [])),\n          \"review\": Array.from(new Set(this.progress.review || [])),\n          \"bookmarked\": Array.from(new Set(this.progress.bookmarked || [])),\n          \"history\": (this.progress.history || []).slice(0, 50),\n          \"notes\": Object.assign({}, this.progress.notes || {}),\n          \"